title: CoffeeLoader Execution via rundll32 and Patched 7z.dll in a Temp Directory
id: 6d1cb07c-04e5-4cca-ad40-8e65586ef0be
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the CoffeeLoader delivery pattern reported in November 2026: an
    NSIS installer drops a trojanized 7z.dll into a temporary directory and
    launches it through rundll32.exe. The DLL is a patched 7-Zip library whose
    code was partly replaced with self-decrypting shellcode implementing the
    Armoury packer, which now performs GPU-assisted decryption through OpenGL
    compute shaders instead of OpenCL.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com/coffeeloader-malware-attack/
    - https://malware.news/t/a-usb-worm-s-second-life-retadup-spreading-coffeeloader/127317#post_1
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/16
tags:
    - attack.t1027
    - attack.t1218
    - attack.t1055
    - attack.t1091
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_rundll32:
        Image|endswith: '\rundll32.exe'
    selection_7z_dll:
        CommandLine|contains: '7z.dll'
    selection_temp_path:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '\Temp\'
            - '\tmp\'
            - '%TEMP%'
    condition: selection_rundll32 and selection_7z_dll and selection_temp_path
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate 7-Zip component registration or installers that stage 7z.dll under a user or Windows temp directory
    - Software updaters that load a bundled 7-Zip library through rundll32.exe
level: medium
